#!/bin/sh
# The gates that need nothing installed, run before the push rather than after it.
#
# Wired by the root `prepare` script alongside commit-msg (core.hooksPath=.githooks). What it runs is the check
# half of _tools/scripts/prepass.mjs — the repo invariants readable from the checkout alone: test-file coverage,
# the vitest budget every package must name, integration-suite naming, lockfile drift, the fork boundary, the
# release-heading contract, and the gate that a shrunk wire contract pushes with a declared break. No network,
# ~70ms.
#
# ONE OF THEM READS node_modules WHEN IT IS THERE: the .vue templates, which no type checker looks at and only
# the app bundle used to. That gate was born below the `--checks-only` line because its compiler is a
# dependency, which left it out of reach of the very hook that stands between a broken template and main — and
# a broken template is what cost five hours and three red pipelines the day it landed
# (docs/ci-failure-audit.md, class A). A push comes from a working clone, so the compiler is present and the
# ~0.8s for ~400 templates is not worth noticing. Where it is absent (the CI preflight job, which runs before
# its install) prepass says so and moves on rather than failing for a tool nobody promised it.
#
# It is here because of what those failures cost in CI. Measured over 40 main pipelines, 10 of the 22 red ones
# died on one of these three, every one of them AFTER `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` had resolved 1,800+
# packages against the registry — 0.6-2.0 min, in four jobs at once, to report something readable from two files
# in the working tree. The preflight job in .github/workflows/ci.yml is the same check on the other side of the push; this
# one is what keeps the round trip from happening at all.
#
# The byte scan rides along for the same reason and at the same price: 4,300 tracked files read in ~120ms, no
# install, no network. It was written after a literal NUL in a string literal turned five source files binary to
# git, grep and every diff viewer — and then sat in `pnpm check` alone, where nothing automatic ever reached it,
# while seven more files picked up the same byte. A gate no hook and no pipeline runs is a comment.
#
# The daemon's two structural gates ride along on the same terms. verify-invariants.mjs is the invariant
# registry's exhaustiveness: every subsystem under _sandbox/sandbox/src registers a check or says why it has
# none. verify-daemon-boundaries.mjs holds the module seams where they stand: no new module takes the whole of
# Services without handing it on, no new pair of subsystems imports each other's values. Both read the checkout
# and nothing else, in milliseconds; both lived in `pnpm check` alone, and the first was red on main for nine
# subsystems with nothing running it.
#
# No dependency guard, unlike commit-msg: this needs only node, which is the thing running the repo. Use
# `git push --no-verify` when you genuinely mean to push a tree that does not pass.
set -e
node _tools/scripts/prepass.mjs --checks-only
node _tools/scripts/control-chars.mjs
node _tools/scripts/verify-invariants.mjs
exec node _tools/scripts/verify-daemon-boundaries.mjs
